 1789, and the results were breathtaking. In fact, it was a revolutionary moment for France. A year of revolution that lasted only seven days and cost more than 20 million francs ($164 billion).
The following are the reasons why:
- The revolutionary war caused a crisis among the nobility, who had been afraid to speak out against the regime;
- In order to defend themselves against their opponents, they had no alternative but to fight back against those that would overthrow them, or use force to try and win them back;
- During this period, the royalists were not able to follow through with the demands made by the people;
- The revolution also brought about changes that affected the family’s religious beliefs;
- It helped the king to get rid of his enemies, because he could then bring down the revolution with his own hands.
